    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d751">

                <pb facs="0692" n="576" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg576"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 815.51/219.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Minister of Honduras</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 23.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1911-03-04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 4, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge your
                    communication of the 20th ultimo, reciting that pursuant to the convention dated
                    January 10th, 1911, between the Republic of Honduras and the United States of
                    America you have, on behalf of your Government and in accordance with its
                    instructions, made and executed with the American banking group consisting of J.
                    P. Morgan and Company, Kuhn, Loeb and Company, the National City Bank of New
                    York, and the First National Bank of New York, a loan contract dated February
                    15th, 1911; and with the Guaranty Trust Company of New York as fiscal agent a
                    contract securing the said loan, dated the same day.</p>
                <p>I have also the honor to state that these agreements, made pursuant to the
                    provisions of the convention of January 10, 1911, have under date of February
                    20, 1911, been duly and properly filed with the Department of State as provided
                    in their articles 11 and 12, respectively.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>(For <signed>Mr. Knox</signed>:) <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
